  --:FormNotAssigned|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|That NPC is no longer assigned as a Wild Shape form for [&DruidName]. --^ErrorCard|
  --:FormMissing|
    --&ErrorMode|CHOOSE --&ErrorMessage|The selected Wild Shape NPC character no longer exists. --^ErrorCard|
  --:FormNoToken|
    --&ErrorMode|CHOOSE --&ErrorMessage|[b][&RequestedFormName][/b] does not have a usable default token. Assign a default token to that NPC before using it as a Wild Shape form. --^ErrorCard|
  --:FormImageUnavailable|
    --&ErrorMode|CHOOSE --&ErrorMessage|[b][&RequestedFormName][/b] uses a Marketplace or otherwise API-incompatible token image. Roll20 Mod scripts can create tokens only from images uploaded to My Library. Assign that NPC a default token or character avatar using a My Library image, then try again. --^ErrorCard|
  --:DruidTokenUnavailable|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|The script found [$GMDruidTokenCount.Raw] placed token(s) linked to the selected [b][&DruidName][/b] character sheet, including [$GMPlayerPageTokenCount.Raw] on the campaign player page. Place exactly one token linked to that specific sheet on the player page, then try again. --^ErrorCard|
  --:ActiveTokenMissing|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|The token recorded for this Wild Shape state can no longer be found. The character sheet has not been changed. --^ErrorCard|
  --:RestoreStateMissing|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|The original token image was not stored, so automatic reversion cannot safely restore this token. --^ErrorCard|
  --:OriginalImageUnavailable|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|The preserved original token can no longer be found, and Roll20 cannot recreate its image through the Mod API. In DM View, use [b]Force Revert[/b] to clear the recorded state, delete the transformed token, and drag the Druid token back onto the page once. --^ErrorCard|
  --:ReplacementFailed|
    --&ErrorMode|MAIN --&ErrorMessage|[b]Token Replacement Failed[/b][br]Roll20 did not return a usable replacement token. If an extra token appeared, delete that extra token before trying again; the Wild Shape state was not changed. --^ErrorCard|
  --:RulesWhileActive|
    --&ErrorMode|GM_SETTINGS --&ErrorMessage|A Wild Shape state is still active. Revert normally, or use the Force Revert button in DM Settings for that Druid before changing between the 2014 and 2024 rules. --^ErrorCard|
  --:Unauthorized|
    --&ErrorMode|NONE --&ErrorMessage|This Wild Shape menu belongs to another player or requires DM access. --^ErrorCard|
